      "file": "blowdown_tank_temperature.glb",
      "title": "Flash it, vent it, cool it",
      "description": "Boiler blowdown leaves at boiler pressure and saturation temperature. Entering the vented tank tangentially, part of it flashes to steam (released through the vent) and the rest drops to ≈ 100 °C. Cooling water is added so the drain to the sewer stays below the permitted temperature (often ≤ ≈ 40–60 °C, local rules). The tank must never be pressurised: the vent is sized for the flash flow and must not be valved.",
